    "rationale": "Chymotrypsin C is a protective pancreatic protease that promotes degradation of trypsinogen and limits harmful intrapancreatic trypsin activity. Loss-of-function CTRC variants diminish this protective pathway and predispose to chronic pancreatitis. Strongest alternative resolved: Impaired intracellular disposal of activated trypsin could theoretically increase pancreatic injury, but CTRC itself protects primarily by promoting trypsinogen degradation; loss of that extracellular digestive-protease checkpoint permits excessive intrapancreatic trypsin activity."
